# Prompt files are measured input, not prose. `bench.mjs` reads a --prompt-file
# verbatim, and at temperature 0 a single changed byte changes the answer - at
# C1b one trailing newline flipped a case-02 verdict from correct to wrong.
# core.autocrlf would rewrite the blank line inside brief.txt on checkout, so
# these must never be line-ending converted.
evals/prompts/*.txt -text

# Shell scripts run under Git's bash, which reads a CRLF line as a command ending
# in `\r` - so core.autocrlf would break tools/model-trial.sh on the next checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
